  Now assemble final answer: findings ranked, then checklist.

  Ranking (most severe first):

  1. High: Mid-pair load contention never reaches the table (cat 6/7). Arms record load_after and ps_top, but the flag column only reflects the pre-pair gate; on nodes where load swings from 4 to 112 within an hour, a clean-gated pair can run entirely under another user's load and report inflated walls (and slightly affected RSS) with flag "-". No signal in the table.

  2. High: Scorer/record identity ignores harness_sha256 (cat 3/4/11). peptide scorers live in corpus.py; G-V11 adoption checks binary/lib/jar/pin/tools but not the harness; the proof run already adopted records across harness f24d0a69 → 7ab160cd. A mid-run harness fix (history says likely) silently mixes two counting/verification rules in one table; G-V13 can't see it.

